# Pairs with RecoveryNeverFallsOffLog, and reproduces the never-written release
# (#3453) production had until issue #4456 was fixed: it published (Zero, persisted
# checkpoint) for a leaf whose clock is Zero and which holds no row, ahead of and
# independently of its recorded snapshot coverage. A never-written leaf can hold
# an empty snapshot below its checkpoint (the zero-coverage repair captures one),
# so the GC trims past that snapshot's coverage, and the next activation
# rehydrates the snapshot, restarts from its coverage and latches stale over a
# prefix the leaf never owned (#4456). The base bounds the release by coverage.
MODULE: RecoveryNeverFallsOffLogNeverWrittenReleaseUnbounded
TARGET: RecoveryNeverFallsOffLog
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: a never-written leaf releases its block at its persisted checkpoint above the coverage of the snapshot it holds
PERTURBS: PublishPin

--- FIND
          THEN MergePin(l, "zero", NeverWrittenRelease(l))
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: the release ignores the leaf's recorded snapshot coverage.
          THEN MergePin(l, "zero", stCp[l])
--- END
